		TutorialText.TextWrapped = true
		TutorialText.RichText = false
		TutorialText.Text = [=[VALM DEX COMMUNITY PLUGINS

1. CREATE YOUR PLUGIN
Create a file named MyPlugin.lua. The file must return a table with an Init function. Valm calls Init(Api) after the plugin is installed and Dex has restarted.

return {
    Name = "My First Plugin",
    Version = "1.0.0",
    Author = "Your Name",
    Description = "A simple Valm Dex plugin",
    Icon = "rbxassetid://1234567890",
    Init = function(Api)
        local Tab = Api:CreateTab("My Plugin", "rbxassetid://1234567890")
        local Section = Tab:AddSection("Example", "MY FIRST TOOL")
        Section:AddLabel("Plugin loaded successfully")
        Section:AddButton("Test", function()
            Api:Notify("Hello from my plugin", 3)
        end)
    end
}

2. INSTALL FROM GITHUB
Upload the .lua or .luau file to a public GitHub repository. Copy its raw.githubusercontent.com URL, paste it into the URL box on the Add page, and press Add Plugin. A GitHub /blob/ URL is also accepted and converted to a raw URL. The file must end in .lua or .luau.

3. SUPPORTED PLUGIN API
Api:CreateTab(Name, Icon) creates a window and returns a Tab.
Api:Notify(Message, Duration) displays a Valm notification.
Api:GetService(ServiceName) safely gets a Roblox service.
Api:GetLocalPlayer() returns the local Player.
Api:GetTheme() returns a copy of the active theme values.
Api:GetVersion() returns the Valm Dex version.
Api:Copy(Text) copies text when the executor exposes a clipboard function.
Api:RegisterFunction(PluginName, FunctionName, Callback) registers a callable plugin function.
Api:CallFunction(PluginName, FunctionName, ...) calls a registered plugin function.

4. TAB AND SECTION CONTROLS
Tab:AddSection(Name, Subtitle) creates a section.
Tab:SetTitle(Text) changes the plugin window title.
Tab:Close() closes the plugin window.
Tab:Destroy() closes the plugin window.
Section:AddLabel(Text, AllowEdit) adds a label. Its result supports SetValue(Text) and GetValue().
Section:AddParagraph(Title, Description) adds a description. Its result supports SetValue(Text), SetTitle(Text), and SetDescription(Text).
Section:AddHeader(Text) adds a bold header.
Section:AddDivider() adds a theme-colored divider.
Section:AddSpacer(Height) adds vertical spacing.
Section:AddButton(Name, Callback) adds a button.
Section:AddFunction(Name, Callback) adds a button and returns the callback wrapper and button.
Section:AddToggle(Name, Callback) adds a toggle and returns a function that sets its state.
Section:AddSlider(Name, Minimum, Maximum, Default, Callback) adds a slider. Its result supports SetValue(Number) and GetValue().
Section:AddProgressBar(Name, Default, Callback) adds a progress indicator. Its result supports SetValue(Number), GetValue(), and Instance.
Section:AddColorpicker(Name, DefaultColor, Callback) accepts Color3 or a hex color string. Its result supports SetHexValue(Hex) and SetRGBValue(Color3).
Section:AddDropdown(Name, Items, Callback) cycles through options. Its result supports Select(Text), ChangeItems(Items), and GetValue().
Section:AddPlayerDropdown(Name, Callback) cycles through current players.
Section:AddTextArea(Name, DefaultText, Callback) adds a multiline editor. Its result supports SetValue(Text), GetValue(), and Focus().
Section:AddImage(ImageId, Height) adds an image using an asset ID or image URL. Its result supports SetImage(ImageId).
Section:AddTextBox(Name, Callback) calls back with the text and EnterPressed value when focus is lost.
Section:AddKeybind(Name, DefaultKey, Callback) runs the callback when the selected key is pressed.

5. PLUGIN FORMATS
The simple format shown above is recommended. Existing module plugins that return both InitDeps(Dependencies) and Main() are still supported. Plugin source is syntax-checked before installation, while plugin code itself runs with the executor permissions available to Valm Dex.

6. EDITING AND UPDATING
Open Manage Plugins to edit or delete installed files. Editing a plugin saves its source and packaged loader. Installing, editing, or deleting asks whether to restart Dex now or later. Later keeps the file change for the next restart.

SECURITY
A community plugin is executable Lua code. Review its source and only install plugins from authors you trust. A raw GitHub link is not a security guarantee.]=]
